Routine annual physical.

MEDICAL HISTORY

Patient reports a history of hypertension and depression. She states she has been doing well and taking her medications as prescribed. She also reports that she has been stressed at work and has been eating a lot of frozen meals due to lack of time to grocery shop and cook. She denies any headaches or swelling.

SOCIAL HISTORY

Patient reports that she is stressed at work and has been putting in more hours. She reports she has not had time to grocery shop or cook meals.

MEDICATIONS

Patient reports taking lisinopril 5 mg daily.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

• Constitutional: Denies headaches.
• Musculoskeletal: Denies any numbness or tingling in the hands.
• Neurological: Denies any numbness or tingling in the hands.
• Psychiatric: Denies any thoughts of self-harm.

VITALS

Blood pressure in the office today was elevated at 150/85 mmHg.

RESULTS

Results of today's labs are normal.

PHYSICAL EXAM

• Respiratory: Lungs are clear bilaterally. No wheezes, rales, or rhonchi.
• Cardiovascular: Regular rate and rhythm without murmurs. No extra heart sounds.
• Neurological: No focal deficits, equal strength in all extremities. No focal neurologic deficits.
• Musculoskeletal: No swelling in the extremities. No focal tenderness.

ASSESSMENT AND PLAN

Patient reports a history of hypertension. Her blood pressure in the office today is elevated at 150/85 mmHg. I will increase her lisinopril to 10 mg daily. She will follow up in one month.

Patient reports a history of depression. She is currently taking lisinopril 5 mg daily. She reports that she has been doing well and has been compliant with her medications. She also reports that she has been attending therapy weekly. I will continue her current medications and she will continue to follow up with her therapist.

Patient reports a history of carpal tunnel release. She denies any numbness or tingling in her hands. She reports that she is doing well and has had no issues with her right wrist. I will continue to monitor her for any new symptoms.

Patient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan. }}<|eot_id|>
