summary is: {{ CHIEF COMPLAINT

Right groin pain.

SOCIAL HISTORY

• Patient reports that she recently learned that her sexual partner has been having multiple sexual encounters with other people.

MEDICAL HISTORY

• Abnormal pap smear in the past.

VITALS

• No fever or chills noted.

PHYSICAL EXAM

• External genitalia: No external lesions.
• Labia majora and labia minora: Normal.
• Physiological discharge: Normal color and smell.
• Cervical exam: Normal cervix. No cervical motion tenderness. No adnexal tenderness or masses noted.
• Pelvic exam: Normal vaginal wall. No cervical motion tenderness. No adnexal tenderness or masses noted.

RESULTS

• Swabs were taken for std testing.

ASSESSMENT

• Screen for std.

PLAN

• Discussed with patient. Patient is high risk due to abnormal pap smear in the past and the recent discovery of her sexual partner having multiple partners for some period of time.
• We will have her give blood for syphilis, HIV, and hepatitis C. Some of these tests will take longer than others. We will call the patient if we see anything, but if she has not heard anything, she can call us in 3 days for results.
• If everything is normal, we will see her again at her next annual checkup.

Patient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan. }}<|eot_id|>
