summary is: {{ CHIEF COMPLAINT

Right knee pain.

MEDICAL HISTORY

Patient reports ongoing management of rheumatoid arthritis. He was last seen 2 months ago for a right knee injection.

SOCIAL HISTORY

Patient reports that he wears compression socks but they have not been helpful.

MEDICATIONS

Xeljanz 11mg daily, Celebrex 200mg daily.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

Musculoskeletal: Reports right knee pain and swelling.
Cardiovascular: Denies chest pain.
Gastrointestinal: Denies abdominal pain.
Genitourinary: Denies urinary incontinence.
Respiratory: Denies shortness of breath.
Skin: Reports skin lesions on his legs.
Neurological: Denies headaches.
Psychiatric: Denies depression.
Endocrine: Denies diabetes.

PHYSICAL EXAM

MSK: Examination of the right lower extremity reveals normal capillary refill in the toes. The right knee is swollen, with pitting edema. Range of motion is slightly diminished. The knee is hot to touch. 

RESULTS

X-rays of the right knee were ordered.

ASSESSMENT AND PLAN

Patient reports right knee pain and swelling. The pain level is 6 out of 10. The pain has been present for 2 months. The right knee is swollen, with pitting edema. The knee is hot to touch. Range of motion is slightly diminished. 

Medical Reasoning: The patient reports right knee pain and swelling. The pain level is 6 out of 10. The pain has been present for 2 months. The right knee is swollen, with pitting edema. The knee is hot to touch. Range of motion is slightly diminished. He reports that he was last seen 2 months ago for a right knee injection. The injection provided temporary relief, but the pain has returned. The patient reports that he wears compression socks but they have not been helpful. He is currently on Xeljanz 11mg daily and Celebrex 200mg daily.

Patient Education and Counseling: I advised the patient that we will give him another steroid injection today. We will also order an x-ray of the right knee to see where the swelling is coming from. We will set up physical therapy and if nothing helps, we will need to get a surgery consult.

Patient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan.

INSTRUCTIONS

The patient will follow up with his primary care physician. }}<|eot_id|>
