Gregory Thompson is a 34-year-old male who presents to the clinic today for the evaluation of right ankle pain. He states that he was going out to take off the trash when he fell on the ice and he was on the ground and he was being really careful. He was with a friend who was visiting and she had to help him up. He states that he was able to rest it and elevate it last night and it is a little better today, but he is definitely still limping and it is not his normal. He has been able to put a little more weight on it today. He states that he has taken some ibuprofen and it has been helpful.

